# Draw.io Diagrams

Before creating or editing a `.drawio` file, read and follow:

- `../specs/DRAW_IO_STANDARDS.md` — canvas settings, layer/grouping rules, shape libraries per
  diagram type, file/folder naming, and the full LLM authoring + layout/alignment checklist
- `../specs/styles/expertflow.json` — the `expertflow` style preset (palette, shapes, fonts, edge
  styling). This is the single source of truth for visual styling — never hardcode colors/fonts
  inline when the preset already defines a role for them.
- `../templates/` — copy the matching starter template (see the decision tree in
  `DRAW_IO_STANDARDS.md` §5.5) rather than authoring a `.drawio` file from scratch.

This is a Cursor-facing pointer, not a duplicate — `DRAW_IO_STANDARDS.md` is the single canonical
copy, also read by Claude Code via the `drawio-skill` integration described in
[`../README.md`](../README.md). Keep edits in one place.
